 <LayoutItem labelText="Post-Assisted Log Structures (PALS) – woody material of various sizes pinned together with untreated wooden posts driven into the substrate to mimic natural wood accumulations. Used to mimic and promote accumulation of large woody debris (LWD) and are designed to influence hydraulic, hydrologic and geomorphic processes&#xa;&#xa;Beaver Dam Analogues (BDAs) – a permeable, channel-spanning structure with a constant crest elevation, constructed with a mixture of woody debris and fill material to form a pond and mimic the form and function of a natural beaver dam. BDAs are temporary, permeable structures built with or without posts using a combination of locally available woody material sediment and fill material. The design and implementation of BDAs is a simple, non-destructive and cost-teffective method to restore the processes that are responsible for physically complex channel and floodplain habitat." visibility="1" htmlState="0" frame="false" marginY="0" zValue="22" id="" opacity="1" size="284.975,105.89,mm" type="65641" templateUuid="{9c3d6441-e0c8-495d-8f9c-4ed0d39b63ef}" halign="1" referencePoint="0" outlineWidthM="0.3,mm" marginX="0" frameJoinStyle="miter" itemRotation="0" valign="32" uuid="{9c3d6441-e0c8-495d-8f9c-4ed0d39b63ef}" position="316.548,134.353,mm" blendMode="0" positionOnPage="316.548,134.353,mm" excludeFromExports="0" groupUuid="" background="false" positionLock="true">
